<title>SWITZERLAND: CS Holding shares ease at opening.</title>
<headline>CS Holding shares ease at opening.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Swiss financial group CS Holding were under slight pressure in early trading on the Swiss Exchange following news the group would report a net loss in 1996 of around 2.1 billion Swiss francs as a result of switching to a new loss provisioning method.</p>
<p>CS Holding's registered shares were down 25 cents to 136.75 francs at 0905 GMT while other Swiss shares were firmer.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
